Third-party data:
- Current-carrying capacity tables (src/uniwire/registry/data/iz_tables.json) reproduce values
  from the public Spanish technical guide GUIA-BT-19 (tables taken from UNE 20460-5-523:2004),
  cited in the file header (see src/uniwire/registry/data/LICENSES.md).

Optional data package (distributed separately, not covered by the Apache License):
- uniwire-data-iec81346 (packages/uniwire-data-iec81346), installed with
  `pip install "uniwire[iec81346]"`, contains an IEC 81346-2:2019 class table derived from the
  Wikipedia article "IEC 81346" and is licensed under CC BY-SA 4.0 (see its README and LICENSE).

Fonts:
- The PDF output uses Liberation Sans 2.1.5, Regular and Bold, shipped unmodified in the package
  (src/uniwire/render/fonts/LiberationSans-Regular.ttf and LiberationSans-Bold.ttf), from the official
  release https://github.com/liberationfonts/liberation-fonts (liberation-fonts-ttf-2.1.5.tar.gz,
  SHA-256 7191c669bf38899f73a2094ed00f7b800553364f90e2637010a69c0e268f25d0).
  Digitized data copyright (c) 2010 Google Corporation, with Reserved Font Arimo, Tinos and Cousine.
  Copyright (c) 2012 Red Hat, Inc., with Reserved Font Name Liberation.
  Licensed under the SIL Open Font License, Version 1.1 (not under the Apache License); the licence text
  is in src/uniwire/render/fonts/LICENSE. A PDF written with it embeds a subset of the font; the OFL does
  not apply to such documents.
- The documentation theme and the web viewer (viewer/) refer to the Public Sans and JetBrains Mono fonts
  (SIL Open Font License 1.1) served by the uniwire.sh website at /assets/fonts/, and fall back to system
  fonts when built and served on their own.

Used but not bundled:
- The web viewer loads Pyodide (Mozilla Public License 2.0) and CodeMirror 6 (MIT) from public CDNs at run
  time.
- The documentation is built with MkDocs and Material for MkDocs (BSD-2-Clause and MIT).
